note: "a dog has ...": a kind of record in one sentence, with kinds written or worked out from use.
a dog has a name (text) and an age (a number).
a cat has a name, lives (starting at 9), a favorite toy and an owner (a person or nothing).
a person has a name, some pets (starting at an empty list of cats).
an order has a customer, an amount,
    a cost and a paid (yes or no, starting at no).
let rex be a new dog with name "Rex" and age 3.
let ann be a new person with name "Ann".
let tom be a new cat with name "Tom", favorite toy "ball" and owner ann.
add tom to the end of ann's pets.
say rex.
say tom's lives, tom's favorite toy.
say ann's name, "has", the number of items in ann's pets, "cat".
let first order be a new order with customer "Bo", amount 120 and cost 80.
say first order's amount minus first order's cost, first order's paid.
set first order's paid to yes.
say first order.
to describe, for a dog:
    say "[the dog's name] is [the dog's age]".
describe rex.
set tom's owner to nothing.
